  "notes": "Rewrote to avoid full table rewrite. The original ADD COLUMN with DEFAULT random() requires PostgreSQL to evaluate random() for every existing row, causing a complete table rewrite under ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock. The safe approach: (1) add the column as nullable (no rewrite), (2) set the default for future rows. Existing rows will have NULL in the token column. If backfilling existing rows with random values is required, that must be done separately in small batches (e.g., UPDATE order_items SET token = random() WHERE id BETWEEN x AND y) to avoid long-running locks. Added lock_timeout and statement_timeout guards.",
